"text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"title":"Graph","role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/TrussNumbers":{"abstract":[{"text":"The truss decomposition of an undirected graph (Cohen; Wang–Cheng), over its simple graph. An","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge’s truss number is the largest k such that it lies in a subgraph where every edge is in at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"least k − 2 triangles: 2 for an edge in no triangle, k for an edge of a k-clique. Parallel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edges share their simple edge’s number, and a self-loop has none.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/TrussNumbers","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrussNumbers"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/trussnumbers","title":"TrussNumbers","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrussNumbers"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"}}}